  "title": "U.S. Vice President JD Vance Rejects Use of 'War' to Describe U.S.-Iran Conflict",
  "summary": "Vance rejected calling the U.S.-Iran conflict a 'war' and avoided predicting the conflict's resolution by November's midterm elections. He also stated that the U.S. has a responsibility to carry out strikes as Iran continues targeting commercial vessels in the Strait of Hormuz.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Vance stated that the U.S.-Iran conflict is not labeled as a 'war' and steered clear of predicting its resolution by November.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vance emphasized the U.S. has a'responsibility' to carry out strikes because Iran continues targeting commercial vessels in the Strait of Hormuz.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vance's claim highlights the complexity of the conflict and the difficulty in minimizing its intensity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
